WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.343 --> 00:00:19.662
A chilly March wind blew as Patrick suited up for the game at the Scorpions' field.

2
00:00:19.663 --> 00:00:24.479
"Hey, Todd!" He waved at the left fielder, who was warming up with the basemen.

3
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:30.397
Todd grinned at him. "Hi, Patrick. I bet you're glad to see me back on the field!"

4
00:00:30.398 --> 00:00:35.497
Patrick nodded. "Left field is okay, but I'd much rather catch!"

5
00:00:35.498 --> 00:00:41.651
"Mickey did a good job filling in. He's a great addition to the team," Todd said.

6
00:00:41.652 --> 00:00:48.889
Patrick looked down, adjusting his pads. "Yeah," he said. "See you later."

7
00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:52.320
He sprinted toward home plate to warm up with Dell.

8
00:00:52.321 --> 00:00:57.566
"Batter up!" called the umpire a few moments later.

9
00:00:57.567 --> 00:01:04.863
Patrick tried to settle into the familiar place behind the plate, but he felt like all eyes were on him.

10
00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:09.522
Todd wasn't the only one who'd said that Mickey had done a good job as catcher last week.

11
00:01:09.523 --> 00:01:13.963
Plus, Mickey was a fantastic hitter—much better than Patrick.

12
00:01:13.964 --> 00:01:21.312
"I can't mess up today," Patrick thought. He'd spent hours last night preparing for the game by reviewing players' stats.

13
00:01:21.313 --> 00:01:25.051
He probably should have spent just as much time on math.

14
00:01:25.052 --> 00:01:28.607
By the bottom of the seventh inning, the score was tied.

15
00:01:28.608 --> 00:01:32.678
The first Scorpions batter stepped up and swung.

16
00:01:32.679 --> 00:01:36.443
Crack! A single.

17
00:01:36.444 --> 00:01:42.758
The next batter stepped into the box. Patrick flicked his gaze toward first base every few seconds.

18
00:01:42.759 --> 00:01:47.771
Dell couldn't easily see the runner, so it was up to Patrick to watch him closely.

19
00:01:47.772 --> 00:01:52.761
If the runner tried to steal a base, Patrick had to signal Dell quickly.

20
00:01:52.762 --> 00:02:01.746
Before Dell released the pitch, the runner started toward second, taking a long lead. Could Dell turn around and pick him off?

21
00:02:01.747 --> 00:02:08.763
"Not worth the risk," decided Patrick. He signaled for a curve ball, and Dell whipped it in.

22
00:02:08.764 --> 00:02:10.272
"Strike!"

23
00:02:10.273 --> 00:02:14.070
The runner dashed back to first base and took his lead again.

24
00:02:14.071 --> 00:02:18.314
Patrick could see Dell get ready for the pick, waiting for Patrick's signal.

25
00:02:18.315 --> 00:02:24.978
The runner inched closer toward second. He was really pushing it.

26
00:02:24.979 --> 00:02:29.397
Patrick considered trying to pick him off, but the runner was fast.

27
00:02:29.398 --> 00:02:33.484
Patrick knew that a mistake on the field would put the runner on second.

28
00:02:33.485 --> 00:02:38.135
So Patrick signaled the pitch, and Dell delivered the fastball.

29
00:02:38.136 --> 00:02:46.644
Whack! The ball rocketed far out to center field. The runner on first base rounded second and slid into third.

30
00:02:46.645 --> 00:02:52.959
By the end of the inning, the runner had scored. The Scorpions won the game, 5-4.

31
00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:59.300
Patrick was standing in the dugout with some other players when Daniel stalked over.

32
00:02:59.301 --> 00:03:03.210
"What's the matter with you, Patrick?" Daniel demanded.

33
00:03:03.211 --> 00:03:07.690
"That guy was an easy pick. You should have signaled Dell."

34
00:03:07.691 --> 00:03:14.459
Patrick kept his eyes down. Daniel was right. Patrick and Dell should have picked off the runner.

35
00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:19.187
"Everybody makes mistakes," Patrick said in a low voice.

36
00:03:19.188 --> 00:03:24.938
Mickey clapped Patrick on the shoulder. "Shake it off, dude. We'll win the next one."

37
00:03:24.939 --> 00:03:27.926
Patrick shrugged Mickey's hand away.

38
00:03:27.927 --> 00:03:33.693
"Players don't lose," Mickey went on. "Teams lose. It's not your fault."

39
00:03:33.694 --> 00:03:38.016
"Yes, it is my fault." Patrick glared at Mickey.

40
00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:43.513
"I was rusty today. That's from being stuck in left field last week."

41
00:03:43.514 --> 00:03:47.914
Dell looked surprised. "Hey, Patrick. Ease up a little."

42
00:03:47.915 --> 00:03:51.601
"Yeah," Daniel chimed in. "Knock it off."

43
00:03:51.602 --> 00:03:57.178
"It's been a bad day." Patrick sighed. "How about just giving me some space?"

44
00:03:57.179 --> 00:04:03.574
"Sure." Dell shook his head and walked away. Mickey and Daniel went to talk with some other players.

45
00:04:03.575 --> 00:04:09.978
Patrick felt Daniel's old mitt in his bag as he stuffed his other equipment inside.

46
00:04:09.979 --> 00:04:13.975
"This thing is more like an unlucky mitt," he thought.

47
00:04:13.976 --> 00:04:17.554
He should give it to Buff for a chew toy.

48
00:04:17.555 --> 00:04:24.389
Patrick avoided his friends at school the next morning. He felt embarrassed by the way he had acted after the game yesterday.

49
00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:30.554
"But it wasn't all your fault," he thought. Daniel shouldn't have criticized Patrick in front of everyone.

50
00:04:30.555 --> 00:04:41.139
He slid into a seat at an empty lunch table. He shoveled down the cafeteria's "Friday Special" and pulled out his math book.

51
00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:47.773
He had a test in 25—no, 24—minutes, and he definitely wasn't ready for it.

52
00:04:47.774 --> 00:04:53.285
He stared at his textbook. Did anyone really need to know about exponents?

53
00:04:53.286 --> 00:04:57.036
"I need to know or I'll flunk this test," he muttered.

54
00:04:57.037 --> 00:05:04.511
"You're kidding!" Dell's voice suddenly rose from a nearby table. He laughed loudly.

55
00:05:04.512 --> 00:05:10.676
Patrick looked to his left. Most of the members of the baseball team were gathered at the other table, talking to Coach.

56
00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:16.421
Mickey said something, and then Dell laughed loudly again, and motioned toward where Patrick sat.

57
00:05:16.422 --> 00:05:23.840
Patrick's face burned. Were they laughing at him? Maybe they were making fun of him because of his mom's van.

58
00:05:23.841 --> 00:05:28.419
Or, more likely, they were saying that his catching stunk yesterday.

59
00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:34.161
Patrick kept his eyes on his book and pretended he didn't hear them. But it wasn't easy.

60
00:05:34.162 --> 00:05:41.344
They kept talking and laughing loudly. Finally Patrick closed the book in frustration and put his head on top of it.

61
00:05:41.345 --> 00:05:44.056
"Test today?" asked a deep voice.

62
00:05:44.057 --> 00:05:48.652
Patrick raised his head. Coach loomed over him like a skyscraper.

63
00:05:48.653 --> 00:05:52.498
"I was just studying," Patrick said.

64
00:05:52.499 --> 00:05:59.388
Coach glanced at the closed book and raised his eyebrows. "I find it easier to study with my book open."

65
00:05:59.389 --> 00:06:01.209
"I'm just tired."

66
00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:06.640
Coach sat across the table from Patrick. "I heard you were having some problems in math."

67
00:06:06.641 --> 00:06:11.464
"What?" Patrick thought. Coach knew about his math grade?

68
00:06:11.465 --> 00:06:14.464
He glanced at the table where his teammates sat.

69
00:06:14.465 --> 00:06:18.868
Dell was the only one that Patrick had told about his last math quiz.

70
00:06:18.869 --> 00:06:22.713
"I can't believe Dell ratted on me!" Patrick thought.

71
00:06:22.714 --> 00:06:25.980
"The school has a tutoring program," continued Coach.

72
00:06:25.981 --> 00:06:32.359
"And strict rules about athletes' grades. So get some help sooner rather than later.

73
00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:37.699
Another failing quiz grade, Patrick, and you won't be able to play baseball."

74
00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:44.880
Patrick swallowed hard. "I'll do better, Coach. I promise." His face burned again.

75
00:06:44.881 --> 00:06:49.519
The whole team was watching as Coach lectured him about his crummy grades.

76
00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:55.248
"Good!" said Coach as the bell rang. "See you later at practice."

77
00:06:55.249 --> 00:06:57.616
"Yes, sir," said Patrick.

78
00:06:57.617 --> 00:07:03.836
Patrick ignored his teammates at the other table. He was still steaming over how they'd been talking about him.

79
00:07:03.837 --> 00:07:11.337
He broke out in a sweat, and suddenly he could feel the cafeteria's "Friday Special" rising in his stomach.

80
00:07:11.338 --> 00:07:18.884
He clamped a hand over his mouth and ran for the exit.
